  "solution": {
    "text": "Number of ways of selecting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> tickets from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> tickets numbered from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> with replacement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></math><br /><br />Now, the largest number on selected tickets must be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>. Hence, favorable cases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></math><br /><br />Therefore, required probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></mfrac></math>",
